---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const description =
  'What CalcPulse collects (very little), how calculators handle your inputs, and how to reach the site.';
const updated = '2026-11-17';
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy — CalcPulse" description={description} updated={updated}>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 sm:px-6 py-12">
    <nav class="text-sm text-ink-400" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-ink-600">Home</a> <span aria-hidden="true">/</span> Privacy
    </nav>
    <h1 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink-950">Privacy</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-400">Last updated {updated}</p>

    <div class="prose prose-ink mt-6">
      <h2>Calculator inputs</h2>
      <p>
        Everything you type into a calculator stays on the page. The arithmetic is done by JavaScript in
        your browser; no input is submitted, stored, logged or attached to an identifier. Closing the tab
        discards it.
      </p>

      <h2>What the server sees</h2>
      <p>
        This is a static site. The server that delivers it sees the ordinary technical data any web
        request carries: the requested page, an approximate location derived from the connection, the
        browser’s user-agent and the time. Aggregate traffic counts may be kept to know which pages are
        read. Nothing on the site requires an account, and no email address is collected.
      </p>

      <h2>Third parties</h2>
      <p>
        The site loads no advertising network and no analytics script. Two kinds of link can take you
        off it: partner links in a guide, and the link to the download page of the tools a guide
        discusses. Those destinations operate under their own privacy policies, and this site sends
        them nothing beyond the request your click makes.
      </p>

      <h2>Purchases</h2>
      <p>
        This site does not sell anything itself and has no checkout. Paid products it points to are
        delivered by Gumroad, which handles the payment and the receipt; the seller never sees your card
        details. Nothing you type into a calculator is passed to Gumroad or to any partner.
      </p>

      <h2>Your choices</h2>
      <p>
        Because the site holds no account or profile, there is nothing to delete. If you have written to
        the site, that message is kept only as long as needed to answer it, and you can ask for it to be
        removed.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Corrections and privacy questions go to the address listed in the site’s repository profile. If
        you arrived here from a search result, the site footer links to the same pages this policy
        describes.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
